    planId: 'plan-1790165134461-ikkfo',
    taskId: 'task-1790165134417-p29oay',
    version: 1,
    goal: 'The catalog client in src/client.ts gives up the moment a request fails. Add retrying, in two parts.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'First, a new module src/retry.ts exporting a `withRetry` helper. It takes the function to call and an options object, and returns a promise.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- `attempts` is the total number of tries, the first one included, so one means no repeating. It must be an integer of at least one; anything else is a caller mistake, so reject with a RangeError without ever calling the function.\n' +
      '- The function being retried is called with the number of the attempt, counting from one.\n' +
      '- The first successful call wins: its value is the result, and nothing is called again.\n' +
      '- When a call fails and attempts remain, `shouldRetry` decides. It is given the error and the number of the attempt that produced it, and returning false stops immediately. It is optional; when it is not supplied every failure is repeated. It is never consulted after the final attempt, because there is nothing left to decide.\n' +
      '- When the attempts run out, or `shouldRetry` says to stop, the promise rejects with the error from the last call that was actually made.\n' +
      '- There is no waiting between attempts.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Second, make the client use it. `ApiClient` takes an optional second constructor argument, an options object whose `attempts` is passed through to the helper; with no options given a request is still made exactly once. What is worth repeating: a status of 500 or above, and a transport that rejected outright. What is not: a status the server chose below 500, which is a considered refusal and will be the same next time. A body that came back whole but does not parse is also not worth another request — the server already said what it had to say, so the request itself must not be repeated because of it.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'The existing tests in src/client.test.ts pass today and must still pass. Do not change them, and do not change the behaviour they cover.',
    steps: [ [Object], [Object], [Object], [Object], [Object] ],
    status: 'READY',
    createdAt: '2026-09-23T12:05:34.461Z',
    updatedAt: '2026-09-23T12:05:34.461Z'
  }
}
